    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`RateLimiter` is implemented in `solution.py`, and the 19 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass. I did not run a coverage check, so I can't confirm the 90% line-coverage gate. The tests exercise every method and every `ValueError` path, so coverage should be well above that.\n\n- **Validation:** `limit`, `window_seconds` and `cost` are checked as the spec requires, and `bool` values are rejected.\n- **Window:** each client has its own list of accepted requests, and a request exactly `window_seconds` old no longer counts.\n- **Time:** a call with a `now` earlier than the latest seen across all clients raises `ValueError`, and equal times are allowed. A call with an invalid `cost` raises before it can move the clock forward.\n- **`retry_after`:** it walks the client's active requests from oldest to newest and returns the wait until enough have expired for the cost to fit.\n\nTwo of my first test expectations were wrong, not the implementation. I corrected one `retry_after` value, and I fixed a check that queried an earlier time than a previous call.",
